+.. setting:: broker_pool_acquire_timeout
+
+``broker_pool_acquire_timeout``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. versionadded:: 5.6
+
+Default: :const:`None`.
+
+The maximum number of seconds to wait for a connection to become available
+from the broker connection pool when sending a task. When the pool limit
+(:setting:`broker_pool_limit`) has been reached, sending a task blocks until
+a connection is released; this setting bounds that wait.
+
+If set to :const:`None` (the default), sending a task blocks indefinitely
+until a connection becomes available.
+
+If the timeout elapses before a connection is acquired, an
+:exc:`~celery.exceptions.OperationalError` is raised. Consider increasing
+:setting:`broker_pool_limit` or this timeout if that happens frequently.
+
 .. setting:: broker_connection_timeout
 
 ``broker_connection_timeout``
